quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  43,23,"We did not send any warner to a town before you, but its elites said: ‘Surely, we found our fathers following a creed, and we are indeed following in their footsteps.’"
  43,24,"He (the messenger) would say: ‘What! Even if I bring you better guidance than what you found your fathers following?’ They would say: ‘Indeed, we disbelieve in what you have been sent with.’"
  43,25,So We took vengeance upon them. And observe how the end of the deniers was!
  43,26,"When Ibrahim (Abraham) said to his (foster) father and his people: ‘I renounce whatever (gods) you worship,"
  43,27,"except Him, Who originated me. Indeed, He will guide me.’"
  43,28,So he made it (i.e. the monotheistic creed) a lasting word among his posterity so they may always turn back (to Allah).
  43,29,"Rather, I provided for these (Arabs) and their fathers until the Truth (i.e. the Qur’an) and a Manifest Messenger (i.e. Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) came to them."
  43,30,"When the Truth came to them, they said: ‘This is magic, and we indeed disbelieve in it.’"
  43,31,And they said: ‘Why was this Qur’an not sent down to some great man (like a chief or an affluent leader) of the two towns (of Ta’if and Mecca)?’
  43,32,Is it they who distribute the mercy of your Lord? We have dispensed among them (the resources of) their livelihood in the present life and raised some of them above others in rank. (Did We decide this) so that some of them (i.e. the rich) should make fun of others (i.e. the poor)? And your Lord’s mercy is better than anything they accumulate.
  43,33,"Were it not that people might (be tempted to) become one community (of disbelievers), We would have indeed made for those who disbelieve in the Most-Compassionate (Lord) silver roofs for their houses and (silver) stairways by which they ascend;"
